      "writtenOn": "2026-08-26T15:39:40Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Following up on the earlier delimiter thread: `cacheKey.split(\"-\", 2)` assumes `dataspaceName` never contains a hyphen. If it ever does (e.g. dataspace \"my-ds\", schemaSet \"foo\" -\u003e key \"my-ds-foo\"), this splits into dataspaceName\u003d\"my\", schemaSetName\u003d\"ds-foo\" and silently evicts the wrong cache entry rather than failing loudly.\n\nSince this is currently true \"not in our case\" but isn\u0027t enforced anywhere, could we either:\n- use a delimiter that\u0027s guaranteed invalid in dataspace/schema-set names, or\n- add a code comment here documenting the naming constraint this relies on, so it doesn\u0027t silently regress if that assumption changes later.",
      "revId": "443a75806fa3b58a27b5a84e857b5b63309df461",
      "serverId": "14b4e41f-c4e3-4fb9-9955-6a9b5656895a"
